{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:80817","published":"2026-10-12T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-10-29T11:02:25.128330796Z","related":["CVE-2026-19654","CVE-2026-78002"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-19654","CVE-2026-78002"],"summary":"Important: rsyslog security update","details":"The rsyslog packages provide an enhanced, multi-threaded syslog daemon. It supports MySQL, syslog/TCP, RFC 3195, permitted sender lists, filtering on any message part, and fine-grained control over output format.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * rsyslog: A configuration-dependent issue in rsyslog's optional imptcp input module can allow an unauthenticated remote peer to crash rsyslogd (CVE-2026-19654)\n  * rsyslog: rsyslog: Denial of service via heap buffer overflow in RainerScript replace() function (CVE-2026-78002)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"rsyslog","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/rsyslog"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.2102.0-15.el8_10.3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:80817.json"}},{"package":{"name":"rsyslog-crypto","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/rsyslog-crypto"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.2102.0-15.el8_10.3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:80817.json"}},{"package":{"name":"rsyslog-doc","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/rsyslog-doc"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.2102.0-15.el8_10.3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:80817.json"}},{"package":{"name